# Landing Pages & Branding

Landing pages are promoted on **Google and social networks** — both organically and paid — so every page
follows `10-seo-organic` (organic) and `14-paid-marketing` (paid) in addition to this rule.

## Branding first
- Each project has a brand guide in `docs/brand/BRAND-GUIDE.md` (skill: `brand-identity`): positioning, value
  proposition, audience, tone of voice (Hebrew), messaging pillars, logo usage, color palette with accessible
  contrast, typography, imagery style, UI tokens.
- Design tokens in code come from the brand guide + Stitch design; pages never introduce ad-hoc colors/fonts.

## Page structure (one goal per page)
Hero (benefit-led headline + subheadline + one primary CTA + visual) → trust strip (logos, numbers, reviews —
real only) → problem → solution/how it works → benefits → social proof/case study → offer/pricing → FAQ
(objections; `FAQPage` schema) → final CTA → footer with business details, privacy policy, accessibility statement.
Internet-marketing elements on the page itself: clear offer, urgency only if real, WhatsApp click-to-chat, lead
magnet where relevant, exit-intent/secondary CTA used sparingly, sticky mobile CTA.

## Lead capture
- Minimal fields (name + phone; email optional), Israeli phone validation → E.164, consent checkbox (unchecked
  by default) for marketing, honeypot + rate limit.
- Lead → CRM via API/queue with UTM + click IDs + landing slug + consent, deduplicated by phone, then the WhatsApp
  lead engine (welcome message, assignment by group/source, warming).
- Thank-you state with next step; fires `Lead` events (Pixel + CAPI + GA4 + Google Ads) with shared `event_id`.

## Quality bar
Lighthouse mobile ≥ 90 (all four categories), message match with the ad, mobile-first, Hebrew copy proofread,
accessible, A/B tests one variable at a time with results logged in `docs/marketing/experiments.md`.
